hello and welcome to video where a man  who knows nothing about comic books  tells you whether comic book movie is  good or bad uh  the batman came out right and it faced  the unique challenge of you know living  in the shadow of christopher nolan's  dark knight trilogy but here's the good  news not only is the batman good even if  i do have problems with it which we will  get to soon but um it manages to step  out of that shadow in even the smallest  ways for example nolan's batman is  typified by you never seeing him come or  leave he's just there but pattinson's  batman has these iconic footsteps that  you always hear before he arrives out of  the shadows i really loved that more  importantly though the batman really  leads into the detective noir side of  batman stories with clues and leads and  interrogations and mysteries and  conspiracies that sort of thing which i  think is fantastic we've never really  had that not to the extent that we get  it in the batman and i think that really  helps it set it apart tonally and  aesthetically and the feel of the story  the film is also unashamedly a comic  book film one of batman's opening lines  is i am vengeance  and the suit is campy and catwoman has  this literal bella clava with little cat  ears and patterns in his brooding and  dark makeup it's just it's just great  it's very comic booky because all of  this means that the batman just feels  different to the films we've had before  you know so it's a detective neo noir  film but is it a good detective neo noir  film  um sometimes you know sometimes it's  clever like for example there's this  clue where it's like you are el rata and  you figure out that eventually it's a  reference to a website and i didn't pick  that which felt dumb but i should have  but again sometimes it treats batman  like a freaking genius for figuring out  the most basic like  fortune cookie riddles  it is at its heart a functional mystery  and it's a fun ride to go on but i'm not  sure that it's the type of mystery where  if i watched it through again i would  pick up on a whole lot of really cool  details you know that gives me that  second viewing experience which to me  is kind of the test of a really good  mystery i did figure out that renewal  this program created by thomas wayne was  probably a bad thing that it wasn't what  people were saying it was like really  early on in the film but that's not  because like it's too obvious it's  because of the cinematic language  tip if anything is on a newspaper or on  the news in the background of a scene  it's never a coincidence it is always  foreshadowing  the real strength of the film is that  the riddler is a fantastic adversary it  constantly feels like he is a threat  that he is in control and that batman  even if he's figuring stuff out is  always a few steps behind  he consistently has the upper hand i did  have to laugh when they said that the  riddler has like 500 followers you know  can you imagine the riddler doing like a  a ray shadow legend sponsorship in the  middle of one of his like murder  broadcasts you know i'll i'll kill this  man just like y'all killed the heroes in  the castle if you click my link down in  the description the batman isn't really  a whodunit story which kind of  disappointed me because i was under the  impression that because the riddler was  wearing a mask that he was going to be  revealed to be someone um  and that never happened and that's fine  it's more a personal thing i don't think  it needed that but i will mention one  gripe that i have with the riddler  despite thinking that he was a fantastic  antagonist  is that i  really don't like um psychopath villains  where their only way of showing that  they are a psychopath is that they will  suddenly explode in anger and yelling  um you know the the only way that they  show that they're unhinged is that they  can't go a full sentence without going  from one decibel to 100. i loved  moriarty from sherlock and he did that  too but it is a little bit cringy and it  happened a little bit too slingshotty  you know too much back and forth uh for  me in the riddler like the riddler was  the most imposing when he was just that  shape on the bridge at the funeral or  when he was just a curser on a computer  screen going have you figured it out yet  there's a silent coolness to that that's  really threatening that makes him feel  in control and i'm more afraid of people  who look like they're in control  and have the upper hand than people who  seem unhinged you know because unhinged  people you can exploit so i wish they  did more of that but this does lead me  on to another massive strength of the  film it is very cohesive everything in  the film fits together wonderfully the  whole mystery and what is uncovered is  intimately tied to batman's ark and his  desire for vengeance and fixing the city  uh as a way of continuing his father's  legacy in a way grappling with what that  means uh who he is as a wayne and who  his father was and in turn that also  really connected to catwoman's arc which  has a lot to do with vengeance as well  bringing these two characters who are on  similar trajectories kind of into a hit  as they evolve in different ways  catwoman and batman both end up in the  exact same moral position they discover  that falcone is responsible for the  death of a loved one the impetus for  their anger and the question is how do  they deal with that and they deal with  it differently there's this symmetry but  also this dichotomy that's that's quite  interesting so the deeper sense that  everything is really connected means  that it felt well thought through and i  think that's great writing i had a  really positive experience with the film  and there was only really one thing that  when i walked away from the theater and  days on am still thinking about that i  didn't really like was the stuff that  happened after they caught the riddler  and they exposed falcone they got him  arrested by the good cops you know  basically it is then revealed that the  riddler inspired his 500 followers to  destroy gotham city by flooding it  biblical style to wipe away the  corruption but this suddenly turned what  was a subtle neo-noir detective mystery  story into a save the city story  and i didn't gel with that vibe as much  that the sudden escalation in the stakes  didn't sit right with me in this film  but also because batman's arc was kind  of meaningfully finished by this point  he chose to not kill falcone to rise  above vengeance and i'm not sure the  stuff that these final beats did for him  really fit you know catwoman had also  finished iraq just in a negative way  because i have a sense that is kind of  her character  there's the scene  at the end after the flooding has  happened where he gets out of flair and  he has a light in the dark and he leads  these people out in a sort of religious  procession almost and then he's seen in  the light helping people onto stretches  it is a little bit funny  it's again it's a little bit of that  campiness uh it's it's weird to watch in  a way  but  i think for me that felt like a batman  ark for the sequel you know the the ark  for this one was him rising above  vengeance and then him grappling with  what he should actually do in the light  rather than in the dark i think sounds  more like a sequel arc that they should  have developed more it just didn't feel  like the natural culmination of the  story for me but who knows maybe i'm  wrong i also just wasn't a big fan of  the sequel bait with the joker in the  prison it's it's just if you want to  give us the joker just do it in the next  film uh i i've never been big on sequel  vade but none of this means i did not  enjoy the film i really did and i  recommend going to watch it if this is  your sort of thing i will also note that  it's aesthetically just beautiful like  my jaw dropped when i saw bruce wayne's  gothic architecture home it is stunning  the whole film  looks gorgeous it's done so well i don't  know who does that sort of thing but  it's beautiful to watch and it looks so  much nicer than in my opinion any of the  mcu films you know the the last thing  that i want to mention is that there is  this one moment where he's escaping the  police and he jumps off a building and  batman just  totals himself on the bridge  look out for it it is really funny it  seems tonally just way off from the rest  of the film it's like slapstick comedy  ah but i also i did love that he got  beat up as well like he's not invincible  in this film which i think is really  cool he's not untouchable anymore  anyways i give batman a b  out of 10  for batman  bye  also a b for bye
 

